# Provenance for the files in this directory.
#
# role:
#   current             - the baseline the local and CI equivalence/speed
#                          gates compare against.
#   historical          - bartcore-native, superseded by a later recording;
#                          the engine could still reproduce these.
#   historical-classic  - pre-cutover; the classic engine that produced
#                          these is deleted, so they can never be
#                          re-recorded. Permanent evidence of the
#                          classic-to-bartcore cutover (see
#                          docs/design/public-surface.md), not a gate.
#
# rule (P17, going forward): a re-record that changes any recorded draw (a
#   non-bitwise link) must name, in its MANIFEST row or the commit body, the
#   ORACLE establishing the new values are right - an exact-gate re-run with
#   its gap, an SBC arm with its result, an analytic identity, or a
#   cross-implementation check. "The deviation looks like the expected
#   class" is an adjudication, not an oracle; a row relying on it must say
#   so explicitly.
#
# pin site note: inst/tinytest/test-rbart-loop-callback.R carries 15
#   RNG-locked literals (tolerance 1e-8) that tools/regenerate-snapshots.R
#   does NOT cover; it has been hand-regenerated twice (31a4c017, c8f661af).
#
# file                                role                 commit   machine/arch    scenarios
